From 2f7570d89cd45b48678073d56b5d2d5c4d7f4055 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IMD Ember <operator@imdember.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:09:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/18] Wallet pick: keep the session when the picked wallet
 already grants the signed-in address

The owner runs two wallet extensions and was signed out (and asked to sign again) on every pick in
"My wallet", even when the picked wallet holds the same account. An explicit pick now first reads the
picked wallet's already-granted account (eth_accounts, never a prompt). If it is the signed-in address
and no sign-in or retained flow is in progress, the session stays and only the transport changes. A
locked wallet, an empty or failed reply, another address or a newer event switch as before (the old
session is cleaned up); a pick reverted before the reply changes nothing. Owner decision 2026-10-26.

Tests: the Audit1 same-address case now expects the session to stay; new cases for locked and
other-address picks (still switch) and for a pick reverted before the reply. Removing the fast path
fails the new same-address test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
